      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In practice, \"transparency and oversight\" can be a myth, as governments often justify their censorship decisions behind closed doors. When resources are scarce and urgency trumps nuance, practical considerations can lead to decisions that compromise human rights. In moments of crisis, the need for immediate action can masquerade as compulsive rigidity, relegating due process and accountability to secondary concerns.",
      "source": "target",
